.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt DRAGONET 1
.Os Redhot
.Sh NAME
.Nm dragonet ,
.Nm dgn
.Nd TUI file manager for the Redhot suite
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar path
.Nm
.Op Fl -debug
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -yes
.Op Fl -config Ar file
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a terminal-based file manager.
It navigates directories, performs file operations, and dispatches
files to other Redhot applications.
The canonical binary is
.Nm dragonet ;
.Nm dgn
is an alias.
.Pp
Running
.Nm
with no arguments opens the TUI in the current directory.
The full list of headless commands is documented under
.Sx COMMANDS .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -list Op Ar path
List directory contents as a table.
.It Fl -ls-json Op Ar path
List directory contents as JSON.
Equivalent to
.Fl -list Fl -json .
.It Fl -cp Ar src ... dst
Copy files.
Multiple sources require
.Ar dst
to be a directory.
.It Fl -mv Ar src ... dst
Move files.
Same multi-source rule as
.Fl -cp .
.It Fl -rm Ar path ...
Move files to trash.
.It Fl -rm-permanent Ar path ...
Delete permanently.
Requires
.Fl -yes
to confirm.
.It Fl -restore Ar uuid
Restore a trashed item by UUID (from
.Fl -trash-list ) .
.It Fl -trash-list
List trashed items.
.It Fl -mkdir Ar path ...
Create directories.
.It Fl -touch Ar path ...
Create empty files.
.It Fl -dump-config
Print the default configuration to stdout.
.It Fl -selftest
Check the runtime environment.
Exit 0 when required checks pass, 1 otherwise.
.It Fl -version
Print version.
.It Fl -help , Fl -h
Print help.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -config Ar file
Use the given configuration file instead of the default search path.
.It Fl -debug
Enable debug logging to stderr.
.It Fl -dry-run
Plan operations without executing them.
.It Fl -json
Emit JSON where applicable
.Pq Fl -list , Fl -ls-json .
.It Fl -yes
Bypass the confirmation guard for
.Fl -rm-permanent .
.El
.Sh KEYBINDINGS
Navigation uses arrow keys, Home/End, PageUp/PageDown.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm Enter
Open file or enter directory.
.It Cm Backspace
Go to parent directory.
.It Cm Tab
Focus preview pane.
.It Cm Space
Tag or untag the current entry.
.It Cm Esc
Cancel.
.It Cm ^X
Exit.
.El
.Pp
Ctrl-key bindings:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm ^G
Help.
.It Cm ^W
Find within current directory.
.It Cm ^L
Toggle preview.
.It Cm ^B , ^F
History back / forward.
.It Cm ^D
Move entry to trash.
.It Cm ^P
Permanent delete (requires typing YES).
.It Cm ^R
Rename.
.It Cm ^T
Tag toggle.
.It Cm ^A
Tag all in current level.
.It Cm ^N
Create new file.
.It Cm ^O
Open with a custom command.
.El
.Pp
Alt-key bindings:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm M-C , M-V , M-X
Copy, paste, cut.
.It Cm M-E
Edit with $VISUAL/$EDITOR (bypasses Imp).
.It Cm M-M
Create directory.
.It Cm M-S
Create symlink.
.It Cm M-H
Toggle hidden files.
.It Cm M-I
Cycle metadata level.
.It Cm M-B
Bookmarks menu.
.It Cm M-Z
Suspend TUI and open $SHELL.
.It Cm M-U
Undo last operation.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/redhot/dragonet/dragonet.conf
System-wide configuration (Debian, OpenBSD).
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/redhot/dragonet/dragonet.conf
System-wide configuration (FreeBSD).
.It Pa ~/.config/redhot/dragonet/dragonet.conf
User configuration.
.It Pa ~/.config/redhot/dragonet/bookmarks.conf
User bookmarks.
.It Pa ~/.local/state/redhot/dragonet/session.conf
Per-session state (sort, preview, info level).
.It Pa ~/.local/state/redhot/dragonet/history
Navigation history.
.It Pa ~/.local/state/redhot/dragonet/undo.log
Undo journal.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/Trash
XDG trash directory.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
Operation failed.
.It 2
Nothing to do.
.It 3
Lock held by another instance.
.It 4
Configuration error.
.It 5
Precondition failed.
.It 6
Multi-file operation completed with partial failures.
.It 7
Canceled by user.
.It 8
No handler available for the requested file type.
.It 64
Usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Open the TUI in the current directory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dragonet
.Ed
.Pp
Open the TUI in
.Pa /tmp :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dgn /tmp
.Ed
.Pp
List a directory as JSON:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dragonet --ls-json ~/Downloads
.Ed
.Pp
Copy multiple files into a destination directory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dragonet --cp a.txt b.txt ~/target/
.Ed
.Pp
Delete permanently (requires confirmation):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dragonet --rm-permanent --yes ~/tmp/old.log
.Ed
.Pp
Verify the environment:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dragonet --selftest
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr imp 1 ,
.Xr devil 1
